course: dictionary
lesson: 7834
title: Rabies: a dangerous disease
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rabies is a very dangerous illness. Dogs, bats, foxes and raccoons can carry it, and they usually pass it on by biting. «Never touch a bat; some bats carry rabies or similar viruses.»
explain: Rabies attacks the brain and nerves. Without quick treatment it nearly always kills. «Bats can carry rabies, a disease that is deadly once symptoms start but can be prevented with injections given soon after a bite.» So a bite or scratch must be told to an adult straight away and checked by a doctor.
explain: Read the words around rabies to understand it. «Raccoons can bite and carry rabies, so you keep away from them and keep bins closed.» The clues tell you that rabies is something to avoid, not something to play with.
fact: Rabies is a noun. It is the name of a disease.
fact: Rabies is spread mostly by bites from infected animals.
fact: Pets can have a rabies vaccination to protect them, and doctors may run a test to see if someone has rabies.
fact: «A wild animal that walks up to people and seems tame may be sick with it.» Never assume a friendly-looking wild animal is safe.
fact: Rabies can be prevented if injections are given soon after a bite, so always tell an adult.
exercise: What kind of illness is rabies? | A kind of sweet | A harmless cold | *A very dangerous disease | A type of fruit
exercise: «Raccoons can bite and carry rabies, so you keep away from them.» Which animal can carry rabies? | Cloud | Rose bush | Wooden table | *Raccoon
exercise: What should you do after a bite or scratch from an animal? | Wait a week to see if it gets better | Wash it once and forget it | *Tell an adult and see a doctor at once | Hide it and say nothing
test: «A wild animal that walks up to people and seems tame may be sick with it.» What does this sentence warn you to do? | Call it over | Pick it up to take it home | *Keep away from it | Feed it biscuits
test: Which of these is a way pets are protected from rabies? | Rabies alarm | Rabies picnic | *A rabies vaccination | Rabies shampoo
exam: «Bats can carry rabies, a disease that is deadly once symptoms start but can be prevented with injections given soon after a bite.» Why should a bite be treated quickly? | Because it is a happy day | *Because injections given soon after can prevent rabies | Because bats like waiting | Because the bite will heal by itself
